        name: `The Wooten Brothers`,
        sort_time: "2026-09-10 19:30:00",
        end_time_formatted: "2026-09-10 23:59",
        detail: "The Wooten Brothers’ first public performance occurred in Hawaii in 1966 and established their identity as child prodigies. Since then, they have racked up 26 GRAMMY® nominations and 10 GRAMMY® wins for their mastery of R&B, funk, soul, rock ‘n’ roll, classical music, jazz, disco, and boogie. There’s nothing The Wooten Brothers can’t do. For five decades and counting, they’ve been recognized as some of the most innovative musicians in existence and are collectively known as one of the most talented brother bands in the world. \n\nRegi Wooten was only 13 years old when The Wooten Brothers started opening for funk band WAR and 14 years old when they joined Curtis Mayfield on his SUPERFLY tour. \nKeyboardist Joseph Wooten has played with the Steve Miller Band since 1993. \n5-time GRAMMY winner Roy Wooten invented both the Drumitar and the RoyEl keyboard. \nVictor Wooten is a founding member of Bela Fleck and the Flecktones, 5-time GRAMMY winner, and recognized as “one of the top 10 bassists of all time” (Rolling Stone Magazine).",
        location: "Peace Center SW corner of Broad St. and Main St. Downtown Greenville, South Carolina",
