        detail: "Known for their striking bluegrass presence, Sister Sadie earned a regular seat at The Grand Ole Opry and has headlined every major American roots festival. The Nashville sextet released their acclaimed album All Will Be Well in 2025, earning two GRAMMY® nominations for Best Bluegrass Album. \n\nSister Sadie formed accidentally after an electrifying jam session at Nashville’s Station Inn in 2012. \nBand members are Gena Britt (banjo, vocals), Deanie Richardson (fiddle), Jaelee Roberts (guitar, vocals), Dani Flowers (guitar, vocals), Rainy Miatke (mandolin), and Katie Blomarz-Kimball (bass, vocals). \nHailed as a “bluegrass powerhouse ... long overdue for a proper spotlight. The group has been redefining the landscape of bluegrass for more than a decade” (Lily Paszyc, Live for Live Music).",
